1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,840
We have basically no idea what's making that happen,

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,660
but we had to put some kind of label on it,

3
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,460
and that's dark energy.

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,680
There's an analogy that you can kind of think of.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,520
If you imagine yourself holding a ball

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,600
and you throw the ball up in the air

7
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:15,800
and you know that it's going to come back

8
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,720
and land in your hand.

9
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,680
So this is originally what people thought

10
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,720
was happening with the universe,

11
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,900
that it would expand out and it would come back down again.

12
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,560
But what we found was that the universe

13
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:28,500
was expanding faster and faster.

14
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,660
And so that's like if you throw a ball up in the air

15
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:32,740
and then it shoots away from you

16
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:34,120
faster and faster and faster.

17
00:00:34,460 --> 00:00:35,960
It's very counterintuitive.

18
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:37,800
People weren't expecting this result.

